Create one illustration of a Patchouli Knowledge (Touhou Project) fumo-style stuffed plush doll, seated on a simple wooden tabletop. Oversized broad round head, tiny stuffed body, short arms and two stubby legs forward. Deadpan half-lidded embroidered eyes and tiny stitched mouth, fabric bangs and long side locks, frilled crescent-moon cap, bows at cap sides and side locks, ruffled striped dress. Keep unmistakable plush-toy proportions and cloth construction, not a human character. Full doll entirely inside a square frame with breathing room, nearly frontal view. Soft light from the left; simple quiet background. No words, signature, watermark, other dolls, people or extra props. Medium: expressive digital painterly illustration (Chinese hou-tu / 厚涂). Build the doll in broad opaque painted color masses, with clearly visible directional brush strokes wrapping around stuffed forms. Lavender and violet cloth hair and dress, cream face, yellow felt crescent, muted red and blue bows. Separate large light and shadow groups; warm soft daylight and cooler violet shadows. Selective hard edges around embroidered eyes and crescent, soft and lost edges where fabric blends into shadow. Suggest plush nap with selective broken brushwork, not uniform texture overlay. Painterly restrained wooden tabletop and quiet warm-gray background. Rich sculptural volume and purposeful simplified planes; avoid cel-shaded anime rendering, smooth plastic CGI, and photorealistic fur. This is digital thick painting, not exaggerated raised impasto or palette-knife paint.